{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1069891-questions-about-orphans-of-proteus-tips-for-conversion","id":1069891,"title":"Questions about Orphans of Proteus - Tips for Conversion","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-03-28T22:44:02-07:00","id":1069891,"title":"Questions about Orphans of Proteus - Tips for Conversion","content":"Alright so I'm trying to figure out how to use Orphans of Proteus in my current game. I know that the writers are working on an official version, but ultimately I'm going to try to convert a version for my own usage until then and see how well I can manage it until they do. The problem is that it's my players who enjoy playing this group - I myself am not a hundred percent sure what they are going for. Is this legacy a legacy of shapeshifters who constantly take other shapes? Or is it a legacy of people who choose a sort of spirit animal, plant, or mineral and embody that same entity?<br /> <br /> I'd lean on the latter, though a lot of my confusion exists because of the way they did optional attainments for them. I was always curious if the matter attainments gave an additional form on top of the one that they naturally got, or if it was decided that if your focus was to be to transform into Iron then you needed matter and life when you got your next attainment, or if when you got matter it your one choice was 'over written'. Either way, I had a lot of confusion reading through it and wanted advice.<br /> <br /> At the moment, I'm debating between the orphans getting to choose multiple forms (maybe you get your spirit animal, your spirit plant, and your spirit mineral all at once), and their optional attainments tying to those additional forms - or deciding that an Orphan chooses their animal, plant, or mineral when they join the legacy and all of their attainments focusing on that one animal/plant/mineral even if an effect normally wouldn't work towards them (like having speak-to-beasts work towards iron because that's the mineral you chose, or detect substance (matter 1) working to detect bits of the animal/plant in living or dead forms)<br /> <br /> Thoughts? Tips? Advice?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1513-jakondite","name":"Jakondite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-29T00:06:23-07:00","id":1069916,"title":"","content":"The existence of Legacy attainments doesn't stop you from using your own Magic in order to do the same things your attainments do, just through Supernal power.<br /> <br /> In the 1e writeup, it's suggested that perhaps most Mages stuck either with animal, vegetable, or mineral all the way through their Attainment selection, so if you're going to limit their selection, only let them choose one of the three. You don't get for example to choose flower, horses and coal, you get one of the three, so enjoy turning into a Panda.<br /> <br /> Personally I'd ditch the &quot;stick with one form&quot; requirement, or let them change it through a ritual. Otherwise it's just too onerous, and I'd honestly really just use a Spell anyway.<br /> Unless someone's watching, it's really unlikely that Paradox or Dissonance are going to come into play, and if you're worried about someone dispelling your form, you've got bigger problems to deal with than their potential to do so.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12644,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12644-herbertisbestbert","user":"HerbertIsBestBert","date":". 03-29-2017, 03:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12644-herbertisbestbert","name":"HerbertIsBestBert","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12644_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"312"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-29T21:20:01-07:00","id":1070475,"title":"","content":"I'll be honest, I didn't quite understand when I read this what the purpose of stating that people could use magic instead of legacy attainments was. That seems unimportant to the subject matter to me, as does the statement of paradox and dissonance being unlikely issues (even if in the case of growing claws or gills to their normal form that might not entirely be true). What I was trying to get was a feel for the theme that it was going to - such as if the fact that it was one form was somehow important to the theme of the orphans or if the theme's primary focus was shifting in general, rather than embodying a specific entity. I think the answer to how the 1e form worked (one of the three) though helps, thanks <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1513-jakondite","name":"Jakondite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-30T11:05:33-07:00","id":1070753,"title":"","content":"According to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/929259-upcoming-2e-legacies?p=929344#post929344\">this post</a>, Orphans of Proteus recruit among Adamantine Arrows and Mysterium. This implies a lot about their new focus. The former adapt to different animal forms and gain new strengths from their transformations. The latter experience the world with new senses and use their new forms to access normally unreachable places. If their new write-up limits the number of forms they can take I will be very surprised.<br /> <br /> If I made a write-up I would use the following Spells as Attainments:<br /> <br /> First and Second Attainment<br /> Speak With Beasts (Life \u2022) and Heightened Senses (Life \u2022)<br /> Both Attainments spend +1R either on Instant casting or Advanced Duration. The Second Attainment spends +1R for its respective bonus.<br /> <br /> Third Attainment<br /> Transform Life (Life \u2022\u2022\u2022)<br /> It spends +1R on Advanced Duration. You probably also want to give it Instant Casting. If you do, make it the Fourth Attainment. You can fill this slot with:<br /> Knit (Life \u2022\u2022\u2022)<br /> It spends +1R for healing Lethal damage. It can replicate the skin-shedding Attainment from the 1st Edition.<br /> <br /> Fourth Attainment<br /> Shapechange (Life \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)<br /> It spends +1R on Advanced Duration. You probably also want to give it Instant Casting. If you do, make it the Fifth Attainment. You can fill this slot with Transform Life or:<br /> Mend (Life \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)<br /> It spends +1R on an enhancement of your choice. It would be an improved version of the skin-shedding Attainment.<br /> <br /> Fifth Attainment<br /> Regeneration (Life \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)<br /> +2R and the Spell Factors should be enough to make it Indefinite. If you prefer, you can replace this with improved Shapechange or Mend.<br /> <br /> Note that most of these Spells can normally be cast on others, but as Attainments they're for Orphan's personal use. Personally, I think this deserves a minor benefit to balance things out. I'd be happy to give them an extra Reach, but I have no idea if that's legit.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-30T13:53:48-07:00","id":1070843,"title":"","content":"Yeah I was having difficulty myself deciding whether to go on the 'heightened senses' or not, or even body control. I may for my players make one for both sides, but at the moment I went with characters deciding on 'one' form from the beginning - as part of their legacy. They decide they have an attachment to wolves, or snakes, or flowers, or silver, and from then on all the attainments specify interactions with that one thing, or based on the legacy members. I also altered the effects of the spells themselves slightly. I -wanted- to give them a heal at level 2 similar to snake skin, but by default most mages already get a heal-per-mana at life 2 as a utility attainment.<br /> <br /> Here is what I put down so far.<br /> <br /> First: Friend of Nature<br /> Prerequisite: Initiation<br /> Upon being initiated into the legacy, the Orphan of Proteus gains the capability to communicate with any example of their chosen animal, plant, or mineral. The Orphan may communicate with relatives to the chosen form, such as a dog speaking with a wolf, but this is difficult - requiring a Wits + Expression roll in order to convey appropriate language.<br /> <br /> (Reach: Instant)<br /> <br /> Optional: Matter 1<br /> With Matter 1, the Orphan of Proteus may learn to find any example of their chosen form in any form it may appear. This emulates the effects of detect substance, allowing the Orphan to detect any substance - living, dead, or ephemera - of their chosen form. This includes substances created from the form or part of them, such as alligator boots or venom.<br /> <br /> (Reach: Instant)<br /> <br /> Second: Animal Instinct<br /> Prerequisite: Life 2, Gnosis 2<br /> As the Orphan grows, the Orphan begins to understand their place in the animal kingdom. Their mind becomes more feral and more instinctual - their body follows suit. An Orphan of Proteus with this attainment uses the higher of their wits or dexterity to determine defense. This understanding of the animal kingdom is not limited to them, however. They may also emulate the effects of Control Instincts in other creatures. If the instinct in question is one that would naturally be caused by the Orphan of Proteus' chosen form, it ignores withstand.<br /> <br /> (Reach: Instant)<br /> <br /> Optional: Matter 2<br /> By spending at least a scene in mock ritual of his chosen form, the Orphan becomes immune to the natural instances of the form in which he has chosen. This emulates the effect Alchemist's touch, giving the mage immunity to harmful natural effects of their chosen form - such as venom, or thorns. Additionally, this attainment grants any immunities that nature gave the creature itself - such as resistance to cold, toxins, or heat.<br /> <br /> (Reach: Advanced Duration)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1513,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1513-jakondite","user":"Jakondite","date":". 03-30-2017, 05:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1513-jakondite","name":"Jakondite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}